<script>
import { url } from '@abide/abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="Syntax">
        <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`busy(selection, pattern)
ready(selection, pattern)
refresh(selection, pattern)
invalidate(selection, pattern)`} />

        <p>All four take the same two arguments. Called bare, each one means the whole scope; the
        pattern is optional and narrows a keyed selection to the entries whose args match it.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Members">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>Selection</code></td><td><code>{'Reactive<any, any, any, any> | Keyed<any, any, any, any> | Rpc<any, any, any, any> | { tags: string[] }'}</code></td><td>One value, one keyed value — every args key of it — one handler, which is the value behind it, or every entry carrying any of these tags, across values.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>busy</code></td><td><code>(selection?: Selection, pattern?: Partial&lt;Args&gt;) =&gt; boolean</code></td><td>Whether any entry in the selection has work in flight.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>ready</code></td><td><code>(selection?: Selection, pattern?: Partial&lt;Args&gt;) =&gt; boolean</code></td><td>Whether every entry in the selection has a value to serve.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>refresh</code></td><td><code>(selection?: Selection, pattern?: Partial&lt;Args&gt;) =&gt; void</code></td><td>Stale while revalidate, over the selection.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>invalidate</code></td><td><code>(selection?: Selection, pattern?: Partial&lt;Args&gt;) =&gt; void</code></td><td>Marks the selection stale. Nothing loads and nobody is woken until the next read.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Description">
        <p><strong>Any for <code>busy</code>, all for <code>ready</code>.</strong> These are the
        quantifiers under which <code>busy() &amp;&amp; !ready()</code> reads as one sentence:
        anything is loading, and there is not yet everything to show. An aggregate
        <code>error()</code> would have to decide which failure to hand back, so there is no free
        form of it.</p>

        <p>One signal is held per selection, never one per entry, so a page-level spinner over n
        entries reloading together wakes twice rather than 2n times.</p>

        <p><strong>An explicit argument reaches anything; a bare sweep reaches loads.</strong>
        Passing a <code>Reactive</code> is a deliberate act about that one value, but a bare
        <code>invalidate()</code> matches only entries whose producer is a load — catching a
        <code>reactive(0)</code> would be silent data loss. A synchronous derivation is left alone,
        and recomputes from the load it reads.</p>

        <p><code>invalidate</code> is lazy and <code>refresh</code> is eager, and at this width the
        eager one is bounded by what is subscribed. An <code>invalidate()</code> over two hundred
        entries drops two hundred caches and loads none, where a <code>refresh()</code> reloads only
        what something is reading and marks the rest. That makes <code>refresh()</code> the
        reconnect default.</p>

        <p>A selection is scope-bounded as a value is, and a tag with it, so one request can never
        invalidate another's. A <code>global</code> value belongs to no request, so every selection
        that matches it reaches it, including a tag fired inside a request. And a bare
        <code>invalidate()</code> and a bare <code>refresh()</code> on a server each reach every
        <code>global</code> entry in the process, that being the whole of what a bare sweep can
        still touch once the request's own entries die with it.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Examples">
        <Section title="A page-level activity indicator" level={3}>
            <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`{#if busy()}<Spinner/>{/if}`} />
        </Section>

        <Section title="Everything about one row, across values" level={3}>
            <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`invalidate({ tags: [\`customer:\${id}\`] })`} />
        </Section>

        <Section title="Catching up after a reconnect" level={3}>
            <Code language="ts" caption="browser" code={`watch(() => {
    if (online()) refresh()
})`} />
        </Section>
    </Section>

    <Section title="See also">
        <ul>
            <li><a href={url('/values/decide-when-a-value-reloads')}>Reloading</a></li>
            <li><a href={url('/values/load-once-per-set-of-arguments')}>Caching</a></li>
            <li><a href={url('/reference/reactive')}><code>reactive</code></a></li>
        </ul>
    </Section>
</Doc>
